{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5384-1","published":"2026-11-20T10:04:37Z","modified":"2026-11-21T10:00:04.710559653Z","related":["CVE-2024-58251","CVE-2026-108119","CVE-2026-88829","CVE-2026-88833","CVE-2026-88834","CVE-2026-88842","CVE-2026-90954","CVE-2026-92205"],"upstream":["CVE-2024-58251","CVE-2026-108119","CVE-2026-88829","CVE-2026-88833","CVE-2026-88834","CVE-2026-88842","CVE-2026-90954","CVE-2026-92205"],"summary":"Security update for busybox","details":"This update for busybox fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2024-58251: denial of service via terminal escape sequences (bsc#1241700).\n- CVE-2026-88829: HTTP request smuggling via pipelined requests in httpd reverse proxy (bsc#1285577).\n- CVE-2026-88833: integer underflow in `d4_recv_raw_packet()` when processing untrusted DHCP packets can lead to crash\n  (bsc#1285315).\n- CVE-2026-88834: missing `else` clause after a failed `getspnam_r()` call creates an observable behavioral difference\n  between authentication failures for existing and non-existing system users (bsc#1285314).\n- CVE-2026-88842: dpkg stale field_start pointer causes out-of-bounds read and status file corruption (bsc#1285579).\n- CVE-2026-90954: dpkg-deb extraction-root escape via per-ar-member deferred symlink flush (bsc#1285581).\n- CVE-2026-92205: lack of proper validation of user-supplied path in libarchive allows attackers to create files in the\n  context of the current user (bsc#1286932).\n- CVE-2026-108119: tar extraction-root escape via deferred symlink/hardlink creation bypasses fix (bsc#1284987).\n\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"busybox","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise High Performance Computing 15 SP4-ESPOS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/busybox&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20High%20Performance%20Computing%2015%20SP4-ESPOS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.35.0-150400.3.26.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"busybox":"1.35.0-150400.3.26.1","busybox-static":"1.35.